---

The AI security pack (src/shield360/ai_security) adapts work from Cisco AI Defense
(https://github.com/cisco-ai-defense), Copyright Cisco Systems, Inc. and its
affiliates, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:

  - mcp-scanner (commit 21a87b4bc818c2e279d9af6cf5b20ed386dfc9b5): the
    tool-description rules are adapted from its YARA rules
    (mcpscanner/data/yara_rules), and the tool-poisoning test corpus reuses
    test vectors from tests/test_yara_rules_coverage.py.
  - adversarial-hubness-detector (commit
    7fbfc5479e77e21ec9df094c416e09f0ee76eae9): the RAG hub-chunk check
    follows its median/MAD hub-rate scoring and cross-cluster spread idea,
    reimplemented for streaming retrieval telemetry.
  - project-quarry (commit eadc6e369038dee43886c4470e1b218da4d9cdf1): the
    multi-turn jailbreak heuristic follows its idea of rules over message
    order with counts.

Changes: patterns re-expressed for this language's regular expressions,
weighted and scored with Shield360's injection scoring; no Cisco code is
included verbatim.
